@cc [owner:philipperolet,label:security;backend] access-control-verbs-documented
Every resource implementing `WithAccessControl` (`getAllowedVerbs`) MUST carry a code contract on
its resource class defining what each of its verbs authorizes.

@cc [owner:philipperolet,label:security;backend] permission-checked-fetch
A resource with permissioning is one implementing `WithAccessControl` (`getAllowedVerbs`).
A method that fetches or lists such resources MUST either:
- return no resource for which `resource.canFetch(auth)` is false, as `canFetch` is defined by that
  class (dropped from a list; `null` or an error for a single fetch); or
- carry `dangerously` in its name (`dangerouslyFetchByModelIds`), or take an option whose name or
  value carries it (`permissionFiltering: "dangerously_skip"`), and say in a comment which check is
  skipped and why.

@cc [owner:fontanierh,label:performance;backend] batched-workspace-deletes
Deleting every row of a workspace from a table listed below MUST issue DELETE statements whose row
count is bounded independently of the workspace size (`destroyAllForWorkspaceInBatches`, fixed-size
id batches, or per-parent deletes such as per conversation or per message chunk), and MUST NOT wrap
the whole deletion in one transaction. Listed tables hold more than 100k rows for a single
workspace in production (read replica, October 2026); a table crossing that threshold MUST be added.

`agent_data_source_configurations`, `agent_mcp_action_output_items`, `agent_mcp_actions`,
`agent_mcp_server_configurations`, `agent_message_consumption_items`, `agent_message_skills`,
`agent_messages`, `agent_step_content_tool_executions`, `agent_step_contents`,
`agent_tables_query_configuration_tables`, `content_fragments`, `conversation_participants`,
`conversation_skills`, `conversations`, `data_source_views`, `data_sources`, `files`, `mentions`,
`messages`, `run_usages`, `runs`, `sandbox_function_invocations`, `sandbox_owners`, `sandboxes`,
`user_conversation_reads`, `user_messages`.
